  "notes": "Official 2024-2025 BCCC catalog program page (\"Program: Transportation and Supply Chain Management, AAS\", printed Program Total 60). Emphasis on supply chain logistics, freight, and maritime transportation systems; provides a pathway to fill a workforce gap in transportation, distribution, maritime, and supply chain industries, with options to obtain industry credentials. Courses qualify students to transfer to a Bachelor of Science degree program in transportation, civil engineering, or supply chain management at a four-year college or university. PHI 106 listed in the sequence \"Meets General Education requirement for this program\". 0-credit Computer Literacy requirement documented here only. BCCC's 2025-2026 catalog program pages were unreachable via research tools (Academic Programs index requires JS; search/sitemap endpoints 403), so 2024-2025 remains the latest machine-readable official catalog.",
